---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Risk analyst turned systems builder — what I do and how I work.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Andrae Williams</h1>
    <p class="lede">Risk · Software · AI</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I read risk signals for a living — fraud, payments, merchant behavior — before I
      started building the software that acts on them. These days that means full-stack
      apps, AI agents, and the local infrastructure to run them without handing everything
      to somebody else's cloud.
    </p>

    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <p>
      Risk analysis taught me to distrust a system until it has been tested against real
      failure. I bring that into software: building agents and tools that have to hold up
      under adversarial or messy conditions, not just the happy path — and running as much
      of it as I can on hardware I control, in a homelab built for local inference.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>A few things I try to hold to, in order:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Understand constraints before proposing a solution.</li>
      <li>Build practical systems, not proofs of concept that stop at the demo.</li>
      <li>Inspect failure modes on purpose, not just the success path.</li>
      <li>Prefer evidence to assumptions — including about my own work.</li>
      <li>Make important decisions reversible.</li>
      <li>Document what broke, not just what shipped.</li>
      <li>Use AI as an implementation multiplier, not a substitute for expertise.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      This is where I work things out in public — organised by <a href="/topics/">topic</a>,
      with the occasional multi-part series, a <a href="/lab/">lab</a> for live experiments,
      a <a href="/projects/">work</a> page for what actually shipped, and a <a href="/resources/">reference library</a>{' '}
      for what I actually reach for. There is no publishing schedule; older entries get updated rather than replaced.
    </p>

    <h2>Provenance</h2>
    <p>
      Projects and lab entries record what was built by AI and which model wrote
      it. Posts are mine. That distinction is deliberate and it is visible on
      every entry that has one.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-head { padding: var(--sp-6) 0 var(--sp-5); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin-bottom: var(--sp-5); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); margin: var(--sp-3) 0; }
  .lede { color: var(--text-1); font-family: var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--sp-6); }
  .prose ul { padding-left: 1.25em; }
  .prose li { margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); color: var(--text-1); }
</style>
